  "body": "Only f9c6bee279dc25ef failed, and it failed before the rule was tested: the execution was unrunnable because the kernel identifier was wrong. The proposer wrote `creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object`, but the known kernels do not include that name; the correct identifier is `open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object` (as used in f56c84718cbee21f and its successful execution). The execution detail says: `MINI_KERNEL_UNKNOWN: no kernel 'creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object'; known: [...]`. So the proposer misread the kernel identifier, not the rule. The rule as written and the code do not part company; the proposal never ran. The rule's words the proposer quoted — 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' — are not implicated. What to build next: correct the kernel name to include the `open:` prefix and rerun the pair. f56c84718cbee21f already moved as expected in the first execution; the second execution's duplicate is not a failure."
